cephalic, infrathalamic, thalamic, and striatal damage</article-title><source>Dev Med Child Neurol</source><volume>45</volume><fpage>207</fpage><lpage>12</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12613779</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b5-ndt-3-173"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bostic</surname><given-names>JQ</given-names></name><name><surname>King</surname><given-names>BH</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Autism spectrum disorders: emerging pharmacotherapy</article-title><source>Expert Opin Emerg Drugs</source><volume>10</volume><fpage>521</fpage><lpage>36</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16083327</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b6-ndt-3-173"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bowles</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name><name><surname>Levin</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Aripiprazole: a new atypical antipsychotic drug</article-title><source>Ann Pharmacother</source><volume>37</volume><fpage>687</fpage><lpage>94</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12708948</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b7-ndt-3-173"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brambilla</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Hardan</surname><given-names>AY</given-names></name><name><surname>di Nemi</surname><given-names>SU</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>The functional neuroanatomy of autism</article-title><source>Funct Neurol</source><volume>19</volume><fpage>9</fpage><lpage>17</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15212111</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b8-ndt-3-173"><citation citation-type="book"><collab>British National Formulary</collab><year>2005</year><publisher-name>British Medical Association and Royal Pharmaceutical Society of Great Britain</publisher-name><publisher-loc>London</publisher-loc></citation></ref><ref id="b9-ndt-3-173"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dratcu</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Olowu</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Hawramy</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Aripiprazole in the acute treatment of male patients with schizophrenia: effectiveness, acceptability, and risks in the inner-city hospital setting</article-title><source>Neuropsychiatr Dis Treat</source><volume>2</volume><fpage>191</fpage><lpage>7</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b10-ndt-3-173"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Frith</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Emanuel Miller lecture: confusions and controversies about Asperger syndrome</article-title><source>J Child Psychol Psychiatry</source><volume>45</volume><fpage>672</fpage><lpage>86</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15056300</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11-ndt-3-173"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gillberg</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Billstedt</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Autism and Asperger syndrome: coexistence with other clinical disorders</article-title><source>Acta Psychiatr Scand</source><volume>102</volume><fpage>321</fpage><lpage>30</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11098802</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12-ndt-3-173"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lauritsen</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name><name><surname>Pedersen</surname><given-names>CB</given-names></name><name><surname>Mortensen</surname><given-names>PB</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title